    },
    {
      "text": "Mix together soy sauce, sake, mirin, and ginger in a large bowl until combined.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/subKT8FMk4foRwYMFWeTycLuP5Q=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-87392-japanese-ginger-pork-step-2-70d284c41b994a6a8a3fe706fd3e105c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/87392/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add sliced pork; stir to coat. Cover the bowl and marinate for about 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JXSsd7L5ylcg__EF9cggUpwYE_4=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-87392-japanese-ginger-pork-step-3-9ec71d0cbb8d4023b16f2dd7496fa418.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/87392/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a large skillet or wok over high heat. Sauté pork in hot oil until browned and cooked through; discard marinade. An instant-read thermometer inserted into pork should read at least 145 degrees F (63 degrees C).",
